/Title (Salinity is the amount of dissolved salt in water. Oysters in the Chesapeake Bay live in brackish water, which contains a mixture of freshwater and saltwater. Salinity can change with changes in the amount of freshwater entering the Bay. Oysters can survive within a range of salinities, but very large or sudden changes can stress them.)
